From 92c66af4c7552be25029cfa79e4eebe6c14ba178 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Berg <gitlab@slipsprogrammor.no>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 00:19:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH i-g-t 11/12] tools/gputop: Do not stop at the first missing GT
 id

The frequency loop stops probing as soon as a GT id is not found,
assuming ids are contiguous. That does not hold for xe: the ids are
computed per tile as tile_id * max_gt_per_tile, plus one for the media
GT, and the driver's configfs interface allows disabling the primary
or the media GT of a device. Disable the primary GT and the loop gives
up at gt0 even though gt1 exists, so the header shows no frequency at
all.

Probe every id up to MAX_GTS instead of breaking on the first miss. The
cost is at most eight openat() calls per header.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-1
Signed-off-by: Erik Berg <gitlab@slipsprogrammor.no>
---
 tools/gputop.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/gputop.c b/tools/gputop.c
index cf80c622f..c65d8b76d 100644
--- a/tools/gputop.c
+++ b/tools/gputop.c
@@ -209,7 +209,10 @@ static char *get_intel_frequencies(int card_fd,
 	int gt;
 	bool first = true;
 
-	/* Read frequencies for each GT, assuming they are numbered sequentially */
+	/*
+	 * Probe every possible GT id. They need not be contiguous: xe computes
+	 * them per tile and GTs can be disabled through configfs.
+	 */
 	for (gt = 0; gt < MAX_GTS; gt++) {
 		unsigned int cur_freq = 0, act_freq = 0;
 		bool has_cur, has_act;
@@ -217,7 +220,7 @@ static char *get_intel_frequencies(int card_fd,
 
 		gt_fd = open_gt_sysfs_dir(card_fd, driver_type, gt);
 		if (gt_fd < 0)
-			break;
+			continue;
 
 		if (driver_type == INTEL_DRIVER_XE) {
 			has_cur = read_freq_value(gt_fd, "freq0/cur_freq", &cur_freq);
-- 
